  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Metropolitan Security Services has $527M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Metropolitan Security Services recorded 163 awards with an average award size of $3.2M, and obligations are up 0.0% year over year. Metropolitan Security Services received obligations across multiple fiscal years, including $187M in FY21, $228M in FY22, $258M in FY23, $504M in FY24, and $527M in FY25. Metropolitan Security Services shows the same $527M total for FY26 to date, reflecting the partial current-year total. Metropolitan Security Services delivers most of its obligations through Security Guards and Patrol Services, which accounts for $527M, while smaller work includes Landscape Architectural Services at $29.4K. Metropolitan Security Services receives the bulk of its buying from the Department of Justice at $514M, with secondary buyers including District of Columbia Courts at $12.5M and the General Services Administration at $202K. This snapshot highlights concentration by buyer and primary market for the vendor in the current fiscal period.",
